{"page":311,"blocks":[{"x":0.10294,"y":0.03212,"w":0.84314,"h":0.01513,"fs":0.01277,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Chapter 6 ■ Quantum Mechanics and Molecular Structure 267"},{"x":0.12254,"y":0.1336,"w":0.39183,"h":0.0916,"fs":0.01277,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"els for both N and O appear at the same orbital ener- gies as they do in their respective elemental gases, N2 and O2. This experimental result demonstrates clearly that the core levels do not participate in chemical bond formation and can be neglected in the MO analysis of bond formation."},{"x":0.53921,"y":0.1336,"w":0.39181,"h":0.0916,"fs":0.01277,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"These examples show that photoelectron spectros- copy is useful in testing theoretical models for bonding because it directly measures ionization energies that can be correlated with theoretical orbital energies through Koopmans’s theorem. These methods are readily ex- tended to polyatomic molecules (see Section 20.5)."},{"x":0.67048,"y":0.26053,"w":0.02706,"h":0.01319,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"g2pz"},{"x":0.12106,"y":0.27565,"w":0.01532,"h":0.109,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Photoelectron count rate"},{"x":0.2029,"y":0.28958,"w":0.02962,"h":0.01197,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"N(ls)"},{"x":0.72178,"y":0.32324,"w":0.017,"h":0.01395,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"N2"},{"x":0.55719,"y":0.3313,"w":0.06469,"h":0.01479,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u2px, u2py"},{"x":0.31862,"y":0.33801,"w":0.02215,"h":0.01235,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"g2s"},{"x":0.44607,"y":0.36442,"w":0.0227,"h":0.01488,"fs":0.01022,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"u2s *"},{"x":0.16961,"y":0.42725,"w":0.49281,"h":0.02299,"fs":0.01022,"n":10,"k":1,"t":"415 405 45 40 35 19 18 17 16 Ionization energy (eV)"},{"x":0.20144,"y":0.42725,"w":0.0218,"h":0.01197,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"410"},{"x":0.37398,"y":0.48984,"w":0.31485,"h":0.01616,"fs":0.01022,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"u2s * * *"},{"x":0.63487,"y":0.49333,"w":0.06359,"h":0.01479,"fs":0.01022,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"g2px, g2py"},{"x":0.1226,"y":0.49684,"w":0.01532,"h":0.109,"fs